  "hivDefinitionTitle": "Defination",
  "hivDefinitionSubtitle": "What is HIV/AIDS and how it affects the immune system",
  "hivDefinitionDesc1": "HIV (Human Immunodeficiency Virus) is a virus that attacks the body’s immune system, specifically the CD4 white blood cells (T cells) that fight off infections.",
  "hivDefinitionDesc2": "Without treatment, HIV can gradually destroy CD4 cells over time and advance to AIDS (Acquired Immunodeficiency Syndrome), which is the most advanced clinical stage of HIV infection.",
  "hivDefinitionDesc3": "With modern antiretroviral therapy (ART), people living with HIV suppress the virus to undetectable levels (Undetectable = Untransmittable or U=U), stay healthy, and live long, normal lives.",
  "hivTransmissionTitle": "Mode of transmission",
  "hivTransmissionSubtitle": "How the virus spreads and debunking common myths",
  "hivTransmissionIntro": "HIV is transmitted through contact with specific body fluids from someone with a detectable viral load:",
  "hivTransmissionItem1": "Unprotected sexual intercourse (vaginal or anal sex without condoms).",
  "hivTransmissionItem2": "Sharing contaminated needles, syringes, tattoo needles, or sharp piercing instruments.",
  "hivTransmissionItem3": "Mother-to-child transmission during pregnancy, childbirth, or breastfeeding (largely preventable through PMTCT care).",
  "hivTransmissionItem4": "Transfusion of unscreened blood (extremely rare due to universal laboratory screening).",
  "hivNotTransmittedTitle": "How HIV is NOT transmitted:",
  "hivNotTransmittedDesc": "HIV cannot survive outside the human body. It is NOT spread through shaking hands, hugging, coughing, sneezing, sharing food or toilets, swimming pools, or mosquito/insect bites.",
  "hivPreventionTitle": "HIV-Prevention",
  "hivPreventionIntro": "Protecting yourself from HIV begins with understanding how the virus is spread. Some of HIV prevention methods are discussed as follows:",
  "hivMethodA": "Abstinence from sex (not having sex), before marriage",
  "hivMethodB": "Being faithful (Decide to one sexual partner) after testing.",
  "hivMethodC": "Consistent and correct use of condom every time you have sex.",
  "hivMethodD": "Not sharing sharp objects with other people and Proper use and removal of sharp objects.",
  "hivAdditionalPreventionIntro": "In addition to above mentioned prevention methods, the following are also used to prevent HIV.",
  "hivMethodE": "Provision of anti-HIV treatment for pregnant women living with HIV to avoid transmission to fetus.",
  "hivMethodF": "Pre-Exposure Prophylaxis- Given for people at high risk of acquiring HIV and it is given before exposure to HIV.",
  "prepDesc": "pre-exposure prophylaxis (PrEP) is HIV medicine taken to prevent the chances of getting HIV infection.. Since PrEP only protects against HIV, condom use is still important for the protection against other STI. It will be provided to people at substantial risk (high risk) of acquiring HIV. This service is available at public health facilities like Health center and Hospital.",
