  "hivQ1Text": "HIV infects and destroys cells of human immune system, making it hard to fight other diseases?",
  "hivQ1Insight": "HIV targets CD4 white blood cells. Without ART treatment, the body loses its natural defenses against opportunistic infections.",
  "hivQ2Text": "Which of the following is/are correct about mode of HIV transmission?",
  "hivQ2OptA": "Unprotected sexual practice",
  "hivQ2OptB": "HIV positive mother to their fetus or child",
  "hivQ2OptC": "Eating together",
  "hivQ2OptD": "A & B",
  "hivQ2Insight": "HIV spreads through specific body fluids (unprotected sex and mother-to-child), but cannot be spread through casual contact like sharing food.",
  "hivQ3Text": "Can HIV be transmitted through mosquito or insect bites, hugging, or sharing toilet seats?",
  "hivQ3Insight": "HIV cannot survive outside human fluids or inside insects. Casual social contact is completely safe.",
  "hivQ4Text": "Within how many hours must Post-Exposure Prophylaxis (PEP) be started after possible exposure to HIV?",
  "hivQ4OptA": "Within 24 hours only",
  "hivQ4OptB": "Within 72 hours (3 days)",
  "hivQ4OptC": "Within 1 month",
  "hivQ4OptD": "PEP is only taken before exposure",
  "hivQ4Insight": "PEP is an emergency medication course that must begin strictly within 72 hours of potential exposure to prevent infection.",
  "hivQ5Text": "Which of the following lubricants are safe to use with latex condoms?",
  "hivQ5OptA": "Petroleum jelly (Vaseline) and baby oils",
  "hivQ5OptB": "Body lotions and butter",
  "hivQ5OptC": "Water-based or silicone-based lubricants only",
  "hivQ5OptD": "Household cooking oils",
  "hivQ5Insight": "Oil-based lubricants weaken and tear latex condoms in under a minute. Only water-based or silicone lubricants are safe.",
  "hivQ6Text": "When a person with HIV takes ART and reaches an undetectable viral load, they cannot transmit the virus sexually (Undetectable = Untransmittable / U=U).",
  "hivQ6Insight": "Decades of evidence confirm Undetectable = Untransmittable (U=U). Regular ART adherence keeps people healthy and prevents transmission.",
